     It seems to be guesswork based on a partial reading of
the sources.  The Oracle has no attack capability, and her
passive counterattack against melee attacks only works when
she's being hit by the hero.  There's no possibility of her
magic missiles hitting anyone else; their damage is applied
or resisted immediately rather than being treated as a zap
which might miss and continue past the hero or be mis-aimed
due to displacement.

     Monster against monster combat supports most passive
counterattacks, such as a floating eye's paralysis, but it
ignores passive magic missiles.  Monsters can hit the Oracle
without any risk at all; she's incapable of injuring them.
I assume that this is an oversight; it's hard to imagine it
being intentional.  But I don't think anyone has ever
bothered to report it as a bug....


